---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import OfficerList from '../components/OfficerList.astro';
import BlockButton from '../components/BlockButton.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Our mission | Mind, Brain, Behavior Society"
  description="Why the Mind, Brain, Behavior Society exists: closing the gap between Dartmouth's brain science students and work in their field."
  path="/mission"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <h1 class="page-title">Our mission</h1>

    <section class="section statement-wrap">
      <hr class="rule" />
      <ul class="statement">
        <li>Foster interdisciplinary exploration and collaboration at the intersection of neuroscience, psychology, and related fields that fall between departments at Dartmouth.</li>
        <li>Advance the understanding of the brain and mind.</li>
        <li>Inspire innovation in these fields by connecting undergraduate students through speaker events, research opportunities, and entrepreneurial initiatives.</li>
      </ul>
      <hr class="rule" />
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-h">Practically speaking</h2>
      <p>
        Finance, consulting, and engineering students at Dartmouth have pipelines: clubs,
        recruiting, and ways to work in their field before graduating. Brain science
        students didn't. The society exists to close that gap.
      </p>
      <p>
        Members are a mix of pre-meds, computer science majors, biomedical engineers, and
        neuroscience, biology, and psychology majors, headed toward medicine, academic
        research, software engineering, and healthcare or biotech consulting. Most people
        can't tell whether a field is for them until they've done some of the work or met
        the people doing it. The events and programs here exist to make that happen.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-h">Since 2025</h2>
      <p>
        Founded in spring 2025; the first events ran in fall 2025. Daniel Jeon (biomedical
        engineering) and Shouka Tavakolian (neuroscience) served as the first president and
        vice president and graduated in spring 2026. Today the society has about 90 members,
        six officers, roughly five events a term, and a neurotech team.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2 class="section-h">Officers, 2026 to 2027</h2>
      <OfficerList />
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p><BlockButton href="/what-we-do">See what we do</BlockButton></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .statement {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    padding-block: var(--s4);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .statement li {
    position: relative;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.45;
    padding-left: 26px;
  }
  .statement li + li { margin-top: var(--s3); }
  .statement li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 12px;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    background: var(--wood);
  }
  p + p { margin-top: var(--s3); }
</style>
